# AVD-AWS-0132: S3 bucket not encrypted with a customer-managed key. Fires on
# four buckets; one entry covers all four since .trivyignore matches by check
# ID, not location, so the state bucket can't be gated separately here.
# Accepted for the three audio buckets (infra/modules/environment,
# main/dev/stage): objects expire after 1 day, SSE-S3 already covers them,
# and a customer-managed key would add ~$1/month per key plus per-request
# charges for no real gain. Accepted 2026-09-18.
# Deferred for the Terraform state bucket (infra/bootstrap/main.tf), tracked
# in #217: it holds infra/shared's remote state with app_password,
# openrouter_api_key and vercel_api_token in plaintext, so an AWS-managed key
# lets any s3:GetObject principal read them; a CMK would add a KMS-grant
# layer and CloudTrail auditability. Deferred, not accepted, since it needs
# KMS grants for every state reader (or plan/apply locks itself out), which
# doesn't belong in a CI-refactor PR. Deferred 2026-09-18.
AVD-AWS-0132

# AVD-AWS-0095: SNS topic not encrypted. infra/shared/shared.tf's budget_alerts
# topic only carries AWS Budgets threshold notifications, no sensitive
# payload. Encrypting it needs a KMS customer-managed key, adding standing
# cost to a topic whose whole purpose is controlling cost. Accepted 2026-09-18.
AVD-AWS-0095

# AVD-DS-0002: no USER in the Dockerfile. lambda/Dockerfile builds on
# public.ecr.aws/lambda/python, which runs as root by design; Lambda's
# isolation boundary is the per-invocation microVM, not the container user, so
# the container-escape scenario this check targets doesn't apply here.
# Accepted 2026-09-18.
AVD-DS-0002
